  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 1269894,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "Test your spatial reasoning and reflexes in *LaunchBox*, a fast-paced puzzle game for the Commodore 64! Published in Magic Disk 64 in 1995, this challenging title tasks you with rearranging a square grid to match a given template. The initial arrangement is scrambled, and it's your job to manipulate the rows and columns to achieve the perfect match.\n\nUsing a joystick, you control a small arrow that navigates the four columns of the square. A single button press shifts the row the arrow is pointing to, bringing you one step closer to the target pattern. But beware – a strict time limit adds intense pressure, demanding quick thinking and precise movements.\n\nThe game’s simple controls belie its addictive gameplay. Switching between horizontal and vertical movement is cleverly achieved by moving the arrow to the right edge of the screen and pressing down on the joystick. *LaunchBox* is a test of focus and dexterity, offering a rewarding challenge for puzzle enthusiasts and Commodore 64 fans alike. Can you beat the clock and launch your way to victory?"
    },
